  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>amoxicillin</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>J01CA04</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, oral dosing <small>(PK_1C_enteral)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Dubbelboer IR et al. 2025</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>healthy cats</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>amoxicillin</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://digital-biosystems.github.io/pharmacolibrary-docs/#/drugs/drug_amoxicillin/Amoxicillin_Dubbelboer2025_cat_3\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>Cl</td><td>0.17</td><td>L/h/kg</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>V d</td><td>0.28</td><td>L/kg</td><td><small>V</small></td></tr><tr><td>C maxPO</td><td>4.3</td><td>mg/L</td><td><small>Cmax</small></td></tr><tr><td>T maxPO</td><td>1.1</td><td>h</td><td><small>tmax</small></td></tr><tr><td>AUC0‐ꚙIV</td><td>62.0</td><td>mg*h/L</td><td><small>AUC∞</small></td></tr><tr><td>k eIV</td><td>0.58</td><td>1/h</td><td><small>kel</small></td></tr><tr><td>t 1/2zIV</td><td>1.2</td><td>h</td><td><small>t1/2z</small></td></tr><tr><td>ka (h−1)</td><td>0.17</td><td>h−1</td><td><small>kabs</small></td></tr></table><h4>About amoxicillin</h4><p>Amoxicillin is a penicillin antibiotic used to treat many bacterial infections, including ear, sinus, respiratory and urinary tract infections, and it is also given in combination to eradicate Helicobacter pylori. It is widely used around the world, is included on the WHO list of essential medicines, and is also approved for veterinary use.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q201928\">Wikidata Q201928</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity,